{"accessible_description":"Three elements of A map through two elements of B into two of the four elements of C. The first and third A-elements share one intermediate and final value; the second follows the other branch.","accessible_name":"Composition of f from A to B and g from B to C","accessible_role":"img","asset_path":"assets/diagrams/composition.tikz","asset_sha256":"ad4d91333bb7d95c341e168381965ada603782bfbcaa2452096d8f1ddd78be04","diagram_id":"functions-diagram-005","file":"content/sets-functions-relations/functions/composition.tex","formal_object_id":"sfr-fun-formal-0034","formula_ids":["projected-formula-0001172","projected-formula-0001173","projected-formula-0001174"],"instance_id":"inst-00025","line":33,"linearization":["Call the three A-elements the first, second, and third A-elements; call the two B-elements B one and B two; and call the four C-elements C one through C four.","Under f, the first and third A-elements share B one as their middle value; the second A-element maps to B two.","Under g, B one maps to C one and B two maps to C two; C three and C four receive no arrow.","The dashed composite arrows therefore send the first and third A-elements to the same element of C, namely C one, while the second A-element goes to C two."],"object_class":"external_diagram_tikz","projection_status":"PASS_FORMAL_OBJECT_BOUND","source_record_id":"projected-external-diagram-0008","source_record_kind":"external_diagram"}
